The statistical methodology implemented here follows published references
(Montgomery; AIAG; NIST/SEMATECH; ASTM; Bissell 1990), cited per formula in
docs/FORMULAS.md. Those references are not distributed with this software.

examples/pistonrings.csv and examples/pistonrings_phase1.csv contain piston-
ring diameter measurements taken from the R package 'qcc' (dataset
'pistonrings'); the measurements originate from Montgomery, Introduction to
Statistical Quality Control. They are included as reference data for
verifying the implementation against published values, not as part of the
licensed software.

examples/gage_rr_aiag.csv contains the example Gage R&R study of the AIAG
Measurement Systems Analysis Reference Manual, 4th ed. (2010), as reproduced
by BPI Consulting, "Three Ways to Analyze a Gage R&R Study" (2015).
examples/gage_rr_thermal_impedance.csv contains the thermal impedance study of
Houf & Burman (1988), as listed in the SAS/STAT 14.1 User's Guide, PROC VARCOMP
Example 121.2. Both are included, with attribution, as reference data for
verifying the implementation against published results, not as part of the
licensed software. Sources and the compared figures: examples/DATASETS.md.

examples/type1_bosch.csv contains the readings of the Procedure 1 worked
example in Robert Bosch GmbH, Booklet 10 "Capability of Measurement and Test
Processes". examples/type1_spcforexcel.csv contains the readings of BPI
Consulting's "Type 1 Gage Study" example (SPC for Excel). Both are included,
with attribution, as reference data for verification, not as part of the
licensed software.
